        | 0x20680000    | 0x206AFFFF  | Reserved 192 KB                                                                                                | &#10060;        |
        | 0x206B0000    | 0x206BFFFF  | VCMP register 64 KB                                                                                            | &#9888; not described |
        | 0x206C0000    | 0x206CFFFF  | MD register 64 KB                                                                                              | &#9989;         |
        | 0x206D0000    | 0x206DFFFF  | DDR test module 64 KB                                                                                          | &#9888; partial |
        | 0x206E0000    | 0x206FFFFF  | Reserved 128 KB                                                                                                | &#10060;        |
        | 0x20700000    | 0x207FFFFF  | L2 Cache Space 1 MB                                                                                            | &#9989;        |
        | 0x20800000    | 0x2080FFFF  | Reserved 64 KB                                                                                                 | &#10060;        |
        | 0x20810000    | 0x2081FFFF  | Reserved 64 KB                                                                                                 | &#10060;        |
        | 0x20820000    | 0x2FFFFFFF  | Reserved 248 MB                                                                                                | &#10060;        |
        | 0x30000000    | 0x3FFFFFFF  | Reserved 256 MB                                                                                                | &#10060;        |
        | 0x40000000    | 0x4FFFFFFF  | Reserved 256 MB                                                                                                | &#10060;        |
        | 0x50000000    | 0x53FFFFFF  | Reserved 64 MB                                                                                                 | &#10060;        |
        | 0x54000000    | 0x57FFFFFF  | Reserved 64 MB                                                                                                 | &#10060;        |
        | 0x58000000    | 0x5BFFFFFF  | SPI FLASH storage space 64 MB                                                                                  | &#10060;        |
        | 0x5C000000    | 0x7FFFFFFF  | Reserved 576 MB                                                                                                | &#10060;        |
        | 0x80000000    | 0xBFFFFFFF  | DDR External DDR device address is empty 1 GB                                                                  | &#10060;        |
        | 0xC0000000    | 0xFFFFFFFF  | Reserved 1 GB                                                                                                  | &#10060;        |

        ## Interrupts (GIC interrupt IDs, data sheet Table 3-16)

        The interrupt controller is the GIC of the Cortex-A9 (96 sources; IDs 0-31 are private to the A9, IDs 32-95 are shared peripheral interrupts, ID = 32 + SPI number). The table is machine-translated in the data sheet: `SSP` is the SPI, `2C` the I2C, `AND` the IR, `HOURS` the SATA. The original Chinese table (user guide v02, Table 3-16) names ID 65 VOIE and ID 72 VEDU (H.264 encoder).

        | ID | Source | ID | Source | ID | Source |
        |----|--------|----|--------|----|--------|
        | 32 | COMMTX[0] | 52 | SATA | 72 | VEDU |
        | 33 | COMMRX[0] | 53 | USB EHCI | 73 | JPGE |
        | 34 | WDG | 54 | USB OHCI | 74 | JPGD |
        | 35 | Timer0 | 55 | CIPHER | 75 | Reserved |
        | 36 | Timer1 | 56 | ETH | 76 | MD |
        | 37 | TIMER2 | 57 | FE PHY | 77 | IVE |
        | 38 | TIMER3 | 58-59 | Reserved | 78 | Reserved |
        | 39 | RTC | 60 | Software interrupt | 79-87 | GPIO0-GPIO8 |
        | 40-43 | UART0-UART3 | 61 | L2CACHE_CHK0_INT | 88 | Reserved |
        | 44 | SPI | 62 | L2CACHE_CHK1_INT | 89 | TEM_CAP_INT (RTC temperature sensor) |
        | 45 | I2C | 63 | L2CACHE_INT_COMB | 90-95 | Reserved |
        | 46 | IR | 64 | A9_PMU_INT0 | | |
        | 47 | AIO | 65 | VOIE | | |
        | 48-49 | Reserved | 66 | HDMI | | |
        | 50 | SFC | 67 | VDP | | |
        | 51 | Reserved | 68-71 | VICAP, VPSS, TDE, VCMP | | |

        UART0-UART3 are PL011s without modem-control or IrDA signals: the data sheet (14.3) lists UART_FR bits [2:0] (CTS/DSR/DCD) and [8] (RI), UART_CR bits [13:12] (OUT1/OUT2) and [2:1] (SIR), the modem interrupt bits [3:0] of UART_IMSC/UART_RIS/UART_MIS/UART_ICR and the UART_ILPR register as reserved. The nUARTRTS/nUARTCTS flow-control bits of UART_CR exist (UART1 has RTS/CTS pins).

        The table names IDs 35-38 Timer0-Timer3 and has no entries for Timer4-Timer7. Section 3.6 says the two timers of a Dual-Timer module share one interrupt line, so each of IDs 35-38 is the line of one Dual-Timer module (Dual-Timer0 = Timer0+1 at 0x20000000, Dual-Timer1 = Timer2+3 at 0x20010000, Dual-Timer2 = Timer4+5 at 0x20130000, Dual-Timer3 = Timer6+7 at 0x20140000); the original data sheet (3.6.1) says each pair shares one base address and one interrupt line.

        &#9989; = registers described; &#9888; partial = partly described (offsets known from vendor U-Boot headers or a sibling chip, many bit meanings and all reset values unknown; the block desc starts with 'Partly described:' and registers/fields whose meaning is guessed say 'Meaning unverified'); &#9888; not described = placeholder only (the block's registers exist only in closed vendor libraries and are not documented anywhere; the map only holds an undocumented-window placeholder, the block desc starts with 'Not described:'). Registers whose desc starts with 'Undocumented:' are known to exist (seen in the vendor boot register table) but their meaning is unknown.
    ";

    eHISI_SFC_350       SFC             @ 0x10010000;
    eHISI_AHCI_SATA     SATA            @ 0x10080000;
    eHISI_HIETH_SF      ETH             @ 0x10090000;
